+++ b/.changeset/compare-experiments-failed-runs.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+---
+'@mastra/core': patch
+---
+
+`compareExperiments` no longer lets failed target runs change scores. Experiment scorers still run on a failed run, with empty output, and some prebuilt scorers rate that perfect; those scores are now left out, matched to their attempt, so a retried item keeps only its successful attempts. Repeated attempts are averaged instead of keeping the last one. A scorer with no scores in one experiment is marked `missingIn` instead of being averaged as 0, and one missing from the candidate sets `hasRegression`. The result includes `failedItems`, a warning names items that newly failed, and the opt-in `maxFailedItemIncrease` fails the check on them.
+
+```ts
+const result = await compareExperiments(mastra, {
+  experimentIdA: baselineId,
+  experimentIdB: candidateId,
+  maxFailedItemIncrease: 0,
+});
+result.failedItems; // { a: 0, b: 3 }
+result.hasRegression; // true
+```
diff --git a/packages/core/src/datasets/__tests__/compare-experiments-failed-runs.test.ts b/packages/core/src/datasets/__tests__/compare-experiments-failed-runs.test.ts
